  450: 		 *	a) offsets 0x000..0x123 are normal memory
  451: 		 *	b) offsets 0x124..0x777 are a device
  452: 		 *
  453: 		 *	1) a read is done from offset 0x100. the page is
  454: 		 *	   added to the dyntrans system as a "RAM" page
  455: 		 *	2) a dyntranslated read is done from offset 0x200,
  456: 		 *	   which should access the device, but since the
  457: 		 *	   entire page is added, it will access non-existant
  458: 		 *	   RAM instead, without warning.
